

# 📄 MVP SPECIFICATION (UPDATED)

## AI Speaking Club (Telegram MVP)

---

# 1. Product Overview

**AI Speaking Club** — Telegram-based English speaking practice platform where users:

* join small group conversations in Telegram voice chats
* receive AI-generated feedback after speaking sessions

---

# 2. Correct Tech Stack (FINAL)

## 🧱 Backend Core

* **Python 3.11+**
* **FastAPI** (main backend framework)
* **Uvicorn** (ASGI server)

---

## 🤖 Telegram Layer

* **aiogram v3** (Telegram Bot Framework)
* Bot runs as part of backend service (same deployment unit for MVP)

---

## 🗄 Database

* **PostgreSQL** (primary database)
* **SQLAlchemy 2.0 (async ORM)**
* **Alembic** (migrations)

---

## ⚡ Async / Background Processing (MVP-light)

* **No Redis required for MVP**
* Simple background tasks via:

  * `asyncio.create_task` OR
  * FastAPI BackgroundTasks

---

## 🎙 Speech Processing

* **OpenAI Whisper API** (speech-to-text)

---

## 🧠 AI Layer

* **OpenAI GPT-4o / GPT-4.1**
* Used for:

  * grammar correction
  * fluency scoring
  * vocabulary suggestions
  * repetition detection

---

## 📦 File Storage (MVP)

* Local filesystem (`/uploads`)
* (Optional later → S3 / GCS)

---

## 🌐 Frontend (optional MVP component)

* Simple landing page:

  * Next.js OR any static builder (Tilda acceptable)
* Purpose: redirect to Telegram bot

---

## 🚀 Deployment (MVP)

* Single service deployment:

  * FastAPI + aiogram in one process or same container
* Docker optional but recommended

---

## 🧪 Testing

* **pytest** — test runner
* **pytest-asyncio** — async tests (services, handlers, DB layer)
* **httpx** — ASGI client for FastAPI route tests (`TestClient`)
* External APIs (**OpenAI**, **Telegram**) — mock or stub in unit tests; no real network calls in default test suite

